# SoPlex at tier T1 — T0 with exactly one handicap removed.
#
# T1 lets the competitor choose its own algorithm, so --int:algorithm=1 is
# gone and nothing else moves. The simplifier stays off and solvemode stays
# at the plain floating-point solve.
#
# The caveat T0 records applies here in reverse and is worth keeping in view:
# SoPlex already switched to the primal by itself part-way through some T0
# solves, so T0 never fully forced the dual. That makes T1 minus T0 an
# *under*-statement of what free algorithm choice is worth against SoPlex —
# some of that value was already inside T0. Against HiGHS, which honours
# simplex_strategy, the same difference is measured cleanly, which is why
# both are run.

-s0
--solvemode=0
-f1e-7
-o1e-7
